mingo de los Tsáchilas This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabi Santa Elena El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except: airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec","Jan","Feb"],"shoulder_green":["Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug"],"inflection":["Aug","Feb","Mar"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-Aug for the Sep-Feb dry peak; 1-2 weeks ahead of Ecuadorian holiday weekends/Carnaval/Semana Santa); fire against the arriving Quito curve when Baños rides as an Andes/Amazon attach","events":["Ecuadorian national holiday weekends (feriados) — domestic-demand spikes","Carnaval (Feb-Mar)","Semana Santa"],"rafting_note":"Pastaza Class III+ year-round; Class IV seasonal (~Aug-May)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Casa del Árbol — Swing at the End of the World","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-attractions/Casa-del-Arbol-Swing/d22150-a19710","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the iconic treehouse swing on the Runtún ridge, launching out over the Tungurahua gorge; entry ~$1, 07:00–19:00, harness-secured, 18+","si":"expedition","blurb":"the iconic treehouse swing on the Runtún ridge, launching out over the Tungurahua gorge; entry ~$1, 07:00–19:00, harness-secured, 18+","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Guided swing/viewpoint tour affiliate or DMC leg (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Pailón del Diablo (Devil''s Cauldron waterfall)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.zoegoesplaces.com/cascada-el-pailon-del-diablo-ecuador/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"is one of Ecuador''s most dramatic waterfalls — roughly 80 m tall with a plunge pool ~20 m deep","si":"expedition","blurb":"is one of Ecuador''s most dramatic waterfalls — roughly 80 m tall with a plunge pool ~20 m deep","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Ruta de las Cascadas day-trip affiliate/DMC (trail entry non-comm.)"},{"name":"Ruta de las Cascadas (bike / chiva)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://southamericabackpacker.com/ruta-de-las-cascadas-banos/","hook":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","si":"expedition","blurb":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","commission":"Bike-hire + guided-route/chiva-tour affiliate (fall/cable fees non-comm.)"},{"name":"Canyoning — Río Blanco","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.geotoursbanios.com/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local adventure-operator booking (Geotours/Ivagatours) — guided-only"},{"name":"Whitewater rafting — Río Pastaza (Class III-IV)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-tours/White-Water-Rafting/d22150-g17-c27534","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local operator + activity affiliate"},{"name":"Mirador Bellavista","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.ecuatouring.com/banos-travel-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","si":"expedition","blurb":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","when":"year-round","commission":"Guided town-and-viewpoint walk affiliate or self-guided add-on"},{"name":"Termas de la Virgen thermal baths (at night)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g312857-d20120113-Reviews-Termas_de_la_Virgen-Banos_Tungurahua_Province.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","si":"romance","blurb":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","when":"year-round","commission":"Entry non-commissionable — monetize spa-hotel room-night + private spa add-on"},{"name":"Luna Volcán / former Luna Runtún — spa with volcano view","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.booking.com/hotel/ec/luna-volcan-adventure-spa.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","si":"romance","blurb":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank; property/wing buyout for weddings"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort (converted monastery)","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/ecuador/samari.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank — future Wellness SI anchor"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the \"Swing at the End of the World\" worth it — and how much?","a":"Yes, and it is cheap — it is the image that put Baños on a million screens. The Casa del Árbol treehouse swing launches you out over the Tungurahua gorge from the Runtún ridge at ~2,600 m; the complex opens 07:00–19:00, entry is ~$1, and staff clip you into a climbing harness on a steel-beam frame.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where can couples soak in thermal baths at night in Baños?","a":"At the Termas de la Virgen, in the town center beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall. Its sulfate-rich pools are heated by Tungurahua, open 05:00–17:00 and again 18:00–22:00, at ~$4 adult entry — the signature romantic-and-restorative Baños ritual, best paired with a volcano-view spa-hotel room-night.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is Baños a genuine wellness and spa destination?","a":"Increasingly, yes — the town''s name literally means \"Baths of Holy Water.\" The anchor is Samari Spa Resort, a 300-year-old former Jesuit monastery on ~10 acres with a heated indoor pool, sauna, Turkish bath, whirlpool and full spa, ranked among Baños''s top hotels — mineral-rich thermal springs fed by Tungurahua''s volcanic heat make Baños a natural wellness base.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wellness-—-future-si"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Baños?","a":"Not urban crime — the load-bearing risk is activity risk. ~88% of Ecuador''s homicides occur in five coastal provinces, and the Andean highlands including Baños run below the homicide rates of many mid-sized US cities; the town''s core product is adrenaline (canyoning, Class III–IV rafting, the swing, highway cycling), so guided-vs-unguided is the whole game.","source":"myecuadorvisa.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Tungurahua volcano dangerous right now?","a":"It is a real, live geohazard held quiet by monitoring — not a decorative caveat. Tungurahua erupted near-continuously 1999–2016, then went quiet; as of mid-2026 IG-EPN reports background/very-low activity with no precursor signals and 24/7 instrument monitoring, so any escalation would trigger alerts well in advance. Re-verify live IG-EPN status before booking.","source":"igepn.edu.ec, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is canyoning or the swing in Baños dangerous?","a":"Both carry real, activity-specific risk that guiding and gear mitigate. Canyoning on the Río Blanco is a guided-only roped waterfall-descent sport (helmet, harness, wetsuit, certified guide); the Casa del Árbol swing is 18+ with a ~220 lb (100 kg) weight limit and requires the operator''s climbing harness every ride. Never freelance either — book reputable operators like Geotours or Ivagatours.","source":"geotoursbanios.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador — The Swing, Waterfalls, Rafting & Thermal Baths | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Baños Ecuador","Casa del Árbol columpio","columpio fin del mundo Baños","Pailón del Diablo","Ruta de las Cascadas","rafting río Pastaza Baños","canyoning Baños","Termas de la Virgen","volcán Tungurahua estado","hoteles con spa en Baños"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Baños de Agua Santa"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Luna Volcán, Adventure SPA (formerly Luna Runtún)","category":"Boutique adventure-spa on Tungurahua''s flank, 30 rooms, 35-ha forest","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; Fora/host-agency on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort","category":"300-yr converted-monastery spa resort, ~10 acres","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; host-agency/Fora on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Casa del Suizo","category":"Amazon-edge Napo River jungle lodge (Ahuano), 75 rooms","mor":"DMC package / luxury-specialist — the Amazon-extend upsell","tier":"$$$-$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-1.3928,"lng":-78.4269}}'::jsonb, 9),
  ('blue-hole-belize', '10S', 'The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole', 'Belize', 'Atolls, walls and the Blue Hole', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Belize', '{"liveaboard","expedition","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Great Blue Hole is 318 m (1,043 ft) across and 124 m (407 ft) deep, near the center of Lighthouse Reef ~70 km (43 mi) off Belize City.","Belize has three coral atolls — Turneffe, Lighthouse Reef, Glover''s Reef — within the UNESCO-listed Belize Barrier Reef Reserve System.","Blue Hole stalactites hang at ~100-140 ft (30-42 m); the dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft with a narrow no-deco window — Advanced cert recommended.","Belize Aggressor III/IV depart Belize City Saturdays, up to 5 dives/day, 24-27 dives on a 7-night charter (39-42 on 10-night).","Whale sharks gather at Gladden Spit (southern Belize) around the full moon March-June."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","marine_vhf":"Channel 16","hyperbaric_chamber":"Belize Chamber Project Ltd, San Pedro (Ambergris Caye) — only DAN-Preferred chamber in Belize, 24/7; hours of boat+air transit from the offshore atolls","advisory_date":"2026-06-18","advisory_codes":"C (Crime) only","book_enabled":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"only Southside Belize City restricted; offshore atolls open","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"no_fly_after_diving":"12h single no-deco dive / 18h multi-day repetitive / 24h recommended buffer before BZE flight home","water":"open Caribbean ocean; no malaria offshore; high sun/sea exposure; DAN dive insurance with evac coverage effectively mandatory"},"timing":{"type":"dive-calendar","dive_calendar":true,"curve_start":"2026-02-15","peak":"March-June (Blue Hole best flat seas April-June)","whale_shark_window":["2026-03-14","2026-04-13","2026-05-12","2026-06-11"],"booking_lead_months":"4-6 (peak charters / full-boat buyouts longer)","shoulder_green_season":"September-November (wet/rougher, off-season fill)","fire_date":"2026-02-01","trigger_date":"2026-02-01","sharpen_note":"sharpen on live tracking — Aggressor charter availability + whale-shark sighting logs; flat-sea onset shifts yearly"},"jewels":[{"name":"The Great Blue Hole (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Blue_Hole","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","blurb":"A near-perfect flooded karst sinkhole near the center of Lighthouse Reef, roughly 70 km off Belize City","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane (Aggressor)"},{"name":"Half Moon Caye Wall + Natural Monument","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","tier":"premier","source":"https://ambergriscaye.com/pages/town/divelighthouse.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","si":"Dive Liveaboards/Tropical Islands","blurb":"is rated by many divers as the single best dive site in Belize","when":"year-round","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane; park fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"The Painted Wall & Quebrada (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"liveaboard","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/kbyg_document/Belize","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane"},{"name":"Turneffe Elbow (Turneffe Atoll)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.divessi.com/en/mydiveguide/divesite/98293","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane or Fora via Turneffe resorts"},{"name":"Glover''s Reef (remote atoll)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards/GEA","when":"March-June","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard lane (scarcity — few boats reach it)"},{"name":"Gladden Spit whale sharks (seasonal, southern Belize)","si_tag":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","tier":"comfort","source":"https://belizescuba.com/diving-snorkeling/whale-sharks/","si":"GEA/Dive Liveaboards","commission":"AFF/day-operator or Fora via Placencia; marine-reserve fee non-commissionable"},{"name":"Tobacco Caye","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora lane (small guesthouse packages)"},{"name":"Long Caye (Lighthouse Reef)","si_tag":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.belizehighcommission.com/areas-of-belize/lighthouse-reef-bz","timing":"March-June","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Tropical Islands/Dive Liveaboards","when":"March-June","commission":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on operator"}],"faq":[{"q":"How many dives do you get on a Belize Aggressor liveaboard trip?","a":"Up to five dives a day — 24–27 dives on a 7-night charter, 39–42 on a 10-night. The Aggressor III/IV depart the Fort George dock in Belize City every Saturday at 6 pm, dive Sunday morning to Friday noon, and reach all three atolls, so the liveaboard converts a long day-boat run into unlimited access to Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe and Glover''s.","source":"aggressor.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"How deep is the Great Blue Hole dive and do you need to be certified?","a":"The dive reaches ~40 m/130 ft — at or beyond the recreational limit — to see the stalactites that hang between roughly 100–140 ft. Bottom time is measured in minutes and nitrogen narcosis is a real factor, so reputable operators strongly recommend or require Advanced Open Water certification. It is a deliberately deep dive, not a beginner novelty.","source":"dive-the-world.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is there to do on the Belize atolls if you don''t dive?","a":"The atoll cayes carry barefoot reef-island character for surface-interval and non-diver days. Tobacco Caye is a few-acre reef caye with snorkel-off-the-dock access; Half Moon Caye is a natural monument with ~4,000 nesting red-footed boobies and an observation tower; Long Caye is the inhabited base camp for Blue Hole and Half Moon Caye dives.","source":"belizeadventure.ca, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on an atoll dive trip?","a":"Offshore remoteness from the chamber. The only DAN-Preferred recompression chamber in Belize is on San Pedro, Ambergris Caye — hours of boat-then-air transit from a hit at Lighthouse Reef (~70 km/43 mi offshore) or Glover''s. Liveaboards carry onboard O2 and run DAN protocols as first response, which is why depth and deco discipline are non-negotiable and DAN insurance with evacuation coverage is effectively mandatory.","source":"ambergriscaye.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How long do you have to wait to fly after diving the Blue Hole?","a":"Plan an 18–24 hour buffer. DAN guidance sets a minimum 12-hour surface interval after a single no-deco dive and a minimum 18 hours after multi-day repetitive diving, which every liveaboard trip is; 24 hours is the recommended general practice. A 7-night Aggressor charter ends diving Friday around noon for a Saturday departure precisely to give that buffer before the BZE flight home.","source":"dan.org, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Great Blue Hole & Belize Atolls Diving — Liveaboard, Lighthouse Reef, Turneffe & Glover''s | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":"en","local_keywords":["Belize Blue Hole liveaboard","diving Lighthouse Reef Belize","Belize Aggressor","Great Blue Hole dive depth","Turneffe Atoll diving","Glover''s Reef liveaboard","Half Moon Caye Wall dive","Belize whale shark diving Gladden Spit","no fly after diving Belize"],"hreflang":["en"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["liveaboard","expedition","tropical"],"ultra":[{"name":"Private full-boat liveaboard charter (Belize Aggressor III/IV buyout)","tier":"ultra","mor":"own-CLIA / TCI Land Agency lane — convertible affiliate->commissioned-agent (the moat)","source":"https://www.aggressor.com/destination/belize"},{"name":"Turneffe Island Resort (luxury all-inclusive dive)","tier":"luxury-ultra","mor":"Fora lane (host-agency IATA) all-inclusive dive package","source":"https://visitturneffe.org/discover/where-to-stay-on-turneffe-atoll/"},{"name":"Gladden Private Island (adjacent, southern Belize)","tier":"ultra","mor":"Fora / own-CLIA depending on channel","source":"https://www.belizeadventure.ca/atolls-of-belize/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"The Belize Atolls & Blue Hole, Belize"},"geo":{"lat":17.3158,"lng":-87.5346}}'::jsonb, 10),
  ('bocas-del-toro-panama', '10S', 'Bocas del Toro, Panama', 'Panama', 'Islands strung on a turquoise thread', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Panama', '{"tropical","diveglobal","romance","adventure"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_text":"Exercise Increased Caution (crime + potential civil unrest)","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"remote_flag":true,"hazards":["riptides (Red Frog)","advanced reef surf breaks (Bluff/Paunch)","water-taxi/boat transfers","dengue/zika/chikungunya","non-potable tap water (bottled only)"],"medical":"Bocas Town private clinic; Changuinola ~3h; Panama City evac ~11h road / short flight. Medical-evac insurance advised.","unrest_history":"State of emergency May-Jun 2025 (protests); lifted 2025-06-29; US personnel prohibition lifted 2025-07-08. Monitor before campaigns.","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/panama","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2025-12-10T13:26:25+00:00"}},"timing":{"peak_windows":["Feb-Mar (driest + best viz + surf peak)","Sep-Oct (driest secondary + low crowds)"],"surf_peak":"Dec-Mar (secondary Jun-Jul)","inflection":"late Nov -> Dec","off_season_fill":["Nov (wettest)","Apr-May","Aug"],"fire_date":["~2026-01-18 (for Feb-Mar peak)","~2026-08-20 (for Sep-Oct peak)"],"note":"Caribbean-Panama inverts the national dry season; driest = Feb-Mar and Sep-Oct."},"jewels":[{"name":"Zapatilla Cays","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://go.bocasdeltoro.travel/destinations/cayos-zapatillas/","hook":"two uninhabited, reef-sheltered cays inside Bastimentos National Marine Park; postcard white sand + snorkeling","si":"tropical","blurb":"two uninhabited, reef-sheltered cays inside Bastimentos National Marine Park; postcard white sand + snorkeling","commission":"day-tour referral + non-commissionable park fee"},{"name":"Starfish Beach (Playa Estrella)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://sallysees.com/beaches-in-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"shallow, glass-clear water full of starfish on Isla Colón''s northwest tip; the archipelago''s most photographed spot","si":"tropical","blurb":"shallow, glass-clear water full of starfish on Isla Colón''s northwest tip; the archipelago''s most photographed spot","commission":"island-hop boat-tour referral"},{"name":"Red Frog Beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.redfrogbeach.com/about","si":"tropical","commission":"Red Frog Beach resort booking + boat transfer"},{"name":"Wizard Beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://mokumsurfclub.com/ultimate-bocas-del-toro-guide/","si":"tropical","commission":"guided walk / surf-school referral"},{"name":"Cayo Coral (Coral Cay)","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.snorkeling-report.com/spot/snorkeling-cayo-coral-bocas-del-toro/","hook":"easy patch reef, 10–12 ft, mooring buoys, floating restaurants alongside. Ideal first-timer snorkel","si":"Dive/Snorkel","blurb":"easy patch reef, 10–12 ft, mooring buoys, floating restaurants alongside. Ideal first-timer snorkel","commission":"dive/snorkel operator referral"},{"name":"Bastimentos National Marine Park reefs","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tourismpanama.com/outdoors-and-nature/nature-parks/national-parks/bastimentos-island/","si":"Dive/Snorkel","commission":"PADI operator package + park fee"},{"name":"Dolphin Bay","si_tag":"Dive/Snorkel","tier":"essential","source":"https://bocastours.com/en/packages/zapatilla-cay-tour","hook":"resident dolphin pods; combines with Zapatilla day tours","si":"Dive/Snorkel","blurb":"resident dolphin pods; combines with Zapatilla day tours","commission":"boat-tour referral (ethical operators)"},{"name":"Bioluminescence night tour","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://a